# Cursor Rules for Zephyr (React + Vite + Tailwind)

- Package manager: pnpm only (no npm/yarn lockfiles). Commands: pnpm install; pnpm dev -- --host --port 1000; pnpm lint; pnpm build.
- Do not edit generated output in dist/; source is under src/.
- Styling: Tailwind-first; reuse primitives in src/components/ui before adding new UI code. Prefer clsx/tailwind-merge helpers in lib/utils.js.
- Routing: defined in src/main.jsx using React Router v6 with lazy-loaded pages and PageLoader fallback. Keep new routes lazy.
- App shell: layout in App.jsx; preserve themeService init and notificationService start/stop patterns.
- Theme: respect bg-background/text-foreground classes and index.css tokens; dark/light/system handled in main.jsx.
- ESLint: config in eslint.config.js (React 18, hooks rules, prop-types off). Always run pnpm lint and pnpm build before finishing to catch errors.
- Build: Vite + @vitejs/plugin-react-swc. Keep fix-chunk-loading plugin and manualChunks logic intact in vite.config.js.
- Analytics: @vercel/analytics already mounted in main.jsx; avoid duplicate mounts.
- Testing: no dedicated test setup detected—if adding tests, clarify framework first.
- Git hygiene: keep env files, logs, caches, and editor cruft out of version control; follow .gitignore.
- General: Use concise responses. Prefer functional components/hooks; keep browser-only APIs behind effects or guards.